{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"1cef review-plan round 1: BLOCK (1 blocker + 5 advisories). B1 [+A1,A5]: quarantine trigger #2 mislabeled container criteria (G3/G4/decomp-shape) as 'not inline-runnable', but codebase reserves that class for ISF only (INLINE_UNADMISSIBLE_CRITERIA=frozenset({'ISF'})); containers carry a DISTINCT admission-runner skip-drift reason 'container-material-unrecoverable' vs ISF's 'not-inline-admissible'. FIX: trigger #2 now CONSUMES the admission runner's own skip-drift verdict (observed=skipped, reason in {not-inline-admissible, container-material-unrecoverable}) instead of re-deriving inline-runnability or inventing a class; AC5 + Scope aligned. A2: dropped unbacked RETRYABLE claim, tied BudgetExceeded-FATAL to the ledger finalize()/reserve() path AC7 exercises. A3: named the two failure signals' sub-step sources (runner reproduction result vs emitter FixtureEmitReport.skipped_unbalanced). A4: idempotent-create not atomic -> map builder dedupes by criterion id (lowest ticket id wins), rare double-create self-healing. Desc 7986 chars, 9 ACs. Re-running review-plan."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788501540608008001,"uuid":"21eab726-ad4a-45e9-9945-df6816180d7d"}